  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nI am not sure whether this is wanted or not, but in the Downloads integration configuration, the \"Limit items per integration\" value seems to include entries hidden by the \"Hide completed torrent under this threshold\" option. That is, if I have 50+ entries in my download client but almost all of them are completed and hidden (because of a 5kiB/s threshold), then nothing appears in the client even if I have some alive recent entries that should show up. Setting the limit to a much higher value worked as a workaround. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nHave N old inactive entries in a download client, and set a threshold to have them hidden (I use 5kb/s). Set the limit number of shown items per integration below N, and add a new torrent. The recent and active torrent is hidden.\n\n### Impact\n\nFar from critical, I could not see anything in my Downloads integration even though I expected some entries; this is mostly confusing, and unsatisfying to set the limit of show items to a huge value when I expect to have at most 5 simultaneously active entries.\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_\n\n### Version\n\n1.36.1\n\n### Installation method\n\nUnraid Apps\n\n### Browser\n\nFirefox",
